# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Cargo.lock policy: this is a binary-producing workspace, so Cargo.lock IS
# committed (reproducible builds of the CLIs). Do NOT ignore it — it is tracked
# on purpose. This comment is here so the choice is explicit.

# --- Proprietary firmware must NEVER be committed --------------------------
# Roland firmware images, ROM/sample data, and anything carved out of an
# installer are copyrighted and stay strictly local. Keep working images under
# firmware/ or dumps/ (any depth) and git will refuse to track them.
firmware/
dumps/
**/firmware/
**/dumps/

# Common raw-image / dump extensions, wherever they land.
*.bin
*.rom
*.img
*.dump
*.svd

# Local extraction scratch directories produced by `fw-extract unpack`.
extracted/
**/extracted/

# Vendor update archives are tar, not *.bin — name the container extensions too
# so an unpacked-in-place updater cannot slip past the *.bin rule above.
*.tar
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.exe
*.dmg

# Ghidra project directories. These embed decompiled proprietary code in
# .rep/ databases, so they are as sensitive as the images themselves.
*_ghidra/
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.lock

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
